do.md and todo/gemini-todo.md are separate development lanes. These are project records rather than a complete prompt transcript.",[611],{"_52":612,"_27":613,"_225":614},"Open the complete guild-game project","https://github.com/JacobStephens2/clowder-and-crest","Full Phaser campaign, fifteen minigame types, assets, native shells and tests. Install package dependencies, then npm run dev; the documented dev port is 3200. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.","More ways to play",[618,619],"distribution",{"_52":623,"_27":624,"_225":625},{"_52":620,"_27":621,"_225":622},"GitHub Releases · iOS","https://github.com/JacobStephens2/clowder-and-crest/releases/tag/v2.7.3","Download — Older v2.7.3 IPA; iOS is not included in v2.8.0. Requires suitable signing and sideloading as described by the author, not direct App Store installation. Not installed in this review.","GitHub Releases · Android","https://github.com/JacobStephens2/clowder-and-crest/releases/tag/v2.8.0","Download — Signed v2.8.0 Android APK for sideloading. This is not a Google Play listing. Installer assets were verified; installation was not tested.",[627],{"_52":628,"_27":597,"_225":629},"Play Clowder & Crest","Browser campaign with mouse/touch minigames. The title screen also offers a spoiler-marked unlocked minigame archive. Android/iOS packaging is included, but native installation has separate platform requirements. Initial asset loading can be slow.",[631],{"_52":632,"_27":608,"_225":-7},"Read the creator’s tool and code credits",[634,635,636,637],"Start a guild and complete an opening job.","Read the tool credits and separate coding lanes.","Inspect one minigame and its dedicated playtest.","Change one job mechanic and check campaign progression and saves.","JacobStephens2 identifies Claude Code as the primary coding and design partner, Codex CLI as a second coding lane, and Gemini CLI as a third. PixelLab, Midjourney, ElevenLabs and Suno supplied different asset types; the repository contains per-agent task files.",[634,635,636,637],{"_52":632,"_27":608,"_19":410},{"_52":628,"_27":597,"_19":236,"_225":629},{"_52":612,"_27":613,"_276":277,"_225":614},{"_52":607,"_27":608,"_225":609},[118,427,651],[646,647],{"_648":623,"_27":624,"_19":333,"_225":650},{"_648":620,"_27":621,"_19":333,"_225":649},"platform","Older v2.7.3 IPA; iOS is not included in v2.8.0. Requires suitable signing and sideloading as described by the author, not direct App Store installation. Not installed in this review.","Signed v2.8.0 Android APK for sideloading. This is not a Google Play listing. Installer assets were verified; installation was not tested.","gemini-cli","example:castle-clash-duel-claude","Castle Clash Duel","Recruit warriors and archers and fight a two-player tactical battle on a tilemap. This complete Phaser prototype pairs Claude Code implementation with Pixel Frog’s Tiny Swords artwork.",{"_21":114,"_23":653,"_25":654,"_108":107,"_90":113,"_265":268,"_262":710,"_9":711,"_246":712,"_20":713,"_34":714,"_221":715,"_215":716},[657,658,659,660,661,662,663,664,665,666,667,668,669,670,671,672,673,674,675,676],{"_50":23,"_54":653,"_56":23,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":654,"_56":25,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":266,"_54":107,"_56":108,"_58":59},{"_50":51,"_52":88,"_54":89,"_56":90,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":263,"_54":264,"_56":265,"_58":87},{"_50":51,"_52":260,"_54":710,"_56":262,"_58":59},{"_50":207,"_52":252,"_253":254,"_62":705,"_56":9,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":247,"_62":702,"_56":246,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":244,"_54":245,"_56":246,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":242,"_54":243,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":237,"_62":697,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":235,"_54":236,"_56":20,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":229,"_62":693,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":227,"_54":228,"_56":34,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":219,"_62":689,"_56":221,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":213,"_62":686,"_56":215,"_58":-7},{"_50":207,"_56":208,"_52":209,"_62":685},{"_50":197,"_56":116,"_52":681,"_73":682,"_83":683,"_34":684,"_202":203,"_204":205,"_57":315},{"_50":51,"_56":309,"_52":310,"_54":680},{"_50":60,"_56":304,"_52":305,"_62":677},[678],{"_52":305,"_27":679},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chongdashu/phaserjs-tinyswords/main/docs/preview.gif","2026-10-20","A still from the creator’s gameplay animation, showing lane combat and castle health.","/GameMap/media/learning/castle-clash-duel-claude.webp","Two opposing castles and small fantasy units fighting along a winding lane, with health counters and a match timer.","https://github.com/chongdashu/phaserjs-tinyswords#implementation-with-agent-skills",[211],[687,688],{"_52":211,"_27":218},{"_52":96,"_27":97},[690],{"_52":691,"_27":684,"_225":692},"Read the creator’s AI attribution","README explains PRD-to-code workflow, asset metadata and UI/test implementation; docs/prd.md and docs/tdd.md are published. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[694],{"_52":540,"_27":695,"_225":696},"https://github.com/chongdashu/phaserjs-tinyswords","Full public/index.html game, Tiny Swords assets, PRD, technical design and UI test harness are included. Open public/index.html in a modern browser. No root LICENSE was found; artwork retains Pixel Frog terms. Do not assume unrestricted reuse.",[698],{"_52":699,"_27":700,"_225":701},"Play Castle Clash Duel","https://vibe-tiny-swords.vercel.app/","Author-linked browser prototype with mouse or touch controls. The local public/index.html loads Phaser 3.70.0 from a CDN.",[703],{"_52":704,"_27":684,"_225":-7},"Read the PRD-to-game workflow",[706,707,708,709],"Play a two-player battle and identify recruitment, movement, attacks and castle victory conditions.","Read the published PRD and technical design before tracing the game’s single-file scene logic.","Inspect the Tiny Swords asset metadata and the custom panels used to handle sprite padding.","Change one unit or UI rule with an agent, then replay the battle and inspect the included test harness.","The creator combined a PRD, technical design and curated asset metadata with three Claude Code skills for Phaser gameplay, tilemaps and frontend testing. Human-made Tiny Swords assets are credited separately; this is a prototype.",[706,707,708,709],{"_52":704,"_27":684,"_19":278},{"_52":699,"_27":700,"_19":236,"_225":701},{"_52":540,"_27":695,"_225":696,"_276":277},{"_52":691,"_27":684,"_225":692},[275,118],"resource:phaser","resource","A browser 2D game framework whose official tutorial covers assets, scenes, animation, input, and collisions.","/resources/",{"_21":118,"_786":96,"_265":787,"_50":788,"_785":719,"_780":779,"_27":777,"_60":789,"_763":790,"_754":791,"_751":792,"_747":196},[724,725,726,727,728,729,730,731,732,733,734,735,736],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_50":23,"_54":96,"_56":786,"_58":-7},{"_50":112,"_54":719,"_56":785,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":783,"_54":784,"_56":265,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":781,"_54":782,"_56":50,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_52":778,"_54":779,"_56":780,"_58":59},{"_50":60,"_52":229,"_62":775,"_56":27,"_58":-7},{"_50":60,"_52":768,"_62":769,"_56":60,"_58":-7},{"_50":207,"_52":761,"_253":749,"_62":762,"_56":763,"_58":-7},{"_50":207,"_52":752,"_253":749,"_62":753,"_56":754,"_58":-7},{"_50":207,"_52":748,"_253":749,"_62":750,"_56":751,"_58":-7},{"_50":51,"_52":746,"_54":196,"_56":747,"_58":91},{"_50":51,"_56":743,"_52":744,"_54":745},{"_50":60,"_56":737,"_52":738,"_62":739},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[740],{"_52":741,"_27":742},"Phaser / Phaser Studio","https://github.com/phaserjs/phaser","identity","Identity & attribution","Official framework and examples organization. README explicitly attributes Phaser logo and characters to Phaser Studio Inc. The organization avatar avoids using a version-4 wordmark on Phaser-3 examples.","Source reviewed","verified","Tracks",false,[89],"dimensions","Development stages",[755,756,757,758,759,760],"stages","Planning","Gameplay & code","Assets & animation","Engines & scenes","Testing","Build & release","Topics",[764,89,765,766,767],"tags","Phaser","JavaScript","Browser games","Arcade Physics","Further reading",[770,771],{"_52":774,"_27":742},{"_52":772,"_27":773},"Official documentation","https://docs.phaser.io/","Framework source",[776],{"_52":229,"_27":777},"https://docs.phaser.io/phaser/getting-started/making-your-first-phaser-game","Why it belongs here","Useful for quickly building browser-testable 2D core loops organized around preload / create / update. In the tutorial, scaled static Arcade Physics objects need their collision bodies refreshed. A visible scene alone does not verify input, restart behavior, or lifecycle handling.","detail","Resource type","Tool","Category","Engines & creation tools","summary","name","engines","tool",[799,800],[764,89,765,766,767],[793,794,795,796,797,798],[113],"plan","code","assets","scene","test","ship",{"_52":774,"_27":742},{"_52":772,"_27":773},{"_802":803},"documents",{"_804":805,"_806":807},"en",[809,813,814,815,812,816,817,818,819,820,821,822,823,824,825,826,827,828,829,830,831,832,833,834,835,836,837,838,839,840,841,842,843,844,845,846,847,811,848,810,849,850,851,852,853,854,855,856,857,858,859,860,861,862,863,864,865,866,867,868,869],"zh",[808,809,810,811,812],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","asset-selection-feedback","visual-evidence-research","visual-feedback-mechanisms","game-development-evaluation","benchmark-reproducibility","gameplay-state-contracts","agent-interface-evidence","catalog-review-coverage","source-revision-notes","communi